    subtitle: 'Merchants of Software Craftsmanship',
    nameMeaning: 'Tamil — "merchant · trader · one who creates value through exchange"',
    h2Name: 'An ancient word for a timeless craft',
    pName1: "Vanikar comes from Tamil, one of the world's oldest living languages — and our founders' native tongue. For millennia, Tamil vanikars sailed distant seas and built trusted trade networks, renowned not just for what they sold, but for the integrity, skill, and relationships behind every exchange.",
    pName2: 'We chose the name because we see software the same way: a fair exchange of value — deep expertise and honest craftsmanship in return for your trust. Like the merchants of old, we build things meant to travel far and last long.',
